WEBVTT

1
00:50:38.882 --> 00:50:48.682
Shot. Hallelujah! Is everyone enjoying the nice weather?

2
00:50:48.682 --> 00:50:52.762
No one is going to say it's too hot, right? We're not going to say that, right?

3
00:50:52.762 --> 00:50:57.762
We've been waiting six months for this, so when it's finally warm, we won't complain, right? Amen?

4
00:50:57.762 --> 00:51:04.362
Hallelujah. Chris may invite you for the teaching on the collections.

5
00:51:09.602 --> 00:51:13.842
Hallelujah. Warm, isn't it?

6
00:51:15.842 --> 00:51:20.482
A little teasing is allowed, right? I do want to say that I love him, right?

7
00:51:20.482 --> 00:51:26.562
Hallelujah. I have a beautiful text to introduce the collections.

8
00:51:26.562 --> 00:51:32.562
Apologies for my voice. Probably a remnant from a flight,

9
00:51:32.562 --> 00:51:36.762
where you share everything through breathing in and out, right?

10
00:51:36.762 --> 00:51:41.362
So, yes, you end up with that too, right? Like a spare gift.

11
00:51:41.362 --> 00:51:51.242
The text for today, Luke 14, verses 28 to 30, from the MBV. Wonderful, it's there.

12
00:51:51.242 --> 00:51:53.962
And it says, Jesus says...

13
00:51:53.962 --> 00:52:02.362
For which of you, wanting to build a tower, does not first sit down and estimate the cost to see if he has enough to complete it?

14
00:52:02.402 --> 00:52:05.962
If he lays the foundation but is not able to finish it,

15
00:52:05.962 --> 00:52:13.722
everyone who sees it will ridicule him and say, 'This man began to build but was not able to finish.'

16
00:52:13.722 --> 00:52:21.402
And yes, this text is often explained that it is important for us to calculate the costs beforehand.

17
00:52:21.402 --> 00:52:29.722
But we are so wonderful as people that we actually do not know where we will be in five years.

18
00:52:29.722 --> 00:52:32.802
And then it is often very difficult to calculate costs.

19
00:52:32.802 --> 00:52:39.722
But when we look at Jesus, He did calculate those costs, for you and for me.

20
00:52:39.722 --> 00:52:47.362
The whole backstory leading up to His coming, leaving heaven, 30 years in Nazareth,

21
00:52:47.362 --> 00:52:54.602
three years of popularity, hatred and slander, the unfathomable deep soul anguish in Gethsemane and the suffering,

22
00:52:54.602 --> 00:53:01.402
towards and on the way to Golgotha and actually the stage on which time and eternity turn.

23
00:53:01.402 --> 00:53:06.522
Jesus had already calculated all these costs.

24
00:53:06.522 --> 00:53:08.842
And he has truly not been laughed at.

25
00:53:08.842 --> 00:53:16.282
And he will truly not hear from the Father, that man started to build, but he could not finish.

26
00:53:16.282 --> 00:53:23.202
It is typical of the statements of Jesus, they touch our imperfection.

27
00:53:23.202 --> 00:53:26.842
I cannot do this. I cannot say this, just like that.

28
00:53:26.842 --> 00:53:30.562
For I do not know where I will be in five years.

29
00:53:30.562 --> 00:53:37.802
But what I do know, and that is the only thing he asks of us, is that we trust him wholeheartedly.

30
00:53:37.802 --> 00:53:41.322
And then he says, everything is possible for those who believe.

31
00:53:41.322 --> 00:53:46.722
This is really typical of the gospel. This is typical of the gospel.

32
00:53:46.722 --> 00:53:50.842
And in the preceding verses, he says, whoever follows me and breaks with his father and his mother,

33
00:53:50.882 --> 00:53:56.762
his wife, his children, his brothers and his sisters, yes even with his own life, cannot be my disciple.

34
00:53:56.762 --> 00:54:02.042
Whoever does not carry his cross and follows me cannot be my disciple.

35
00:54:02.042 --> 00:54:04.442
Impossible task.

36
00:54:04.442 --> 00:54:07.442
But yet it becomes possible in Christ.

37
00:54:07.442 --> 00:54:13.242
For if we die to ourselves, and we give Christ that first place,

38
00:54:13.242 --> 00:54:18.842
then we can truly love our fathers and mothers and our brothers and sisters and friends and children

39
00:54:18.842 --> 00:54:23.642
and everything that comes with it, we can truly love, with the love of Jesus.

40
00:54:23.642 --> 00:54:26.042
And that goes much further.

41
00:54:26.042 --> 00:54:30.042
So it is actually the same with that cost calculation.

42
00:54:30.042 --> 00:54:37.042
For if we trust in Him, who has done the math, and filled in that calculation for me,

43
00:54:37.042 --> 00:54:39.842
then I can do a lot.

44
00:54:39.842 --> 00:54:45.042
I did not receive a red cape from Jesus to go through life as Superman.

45
00:54:45.042 --> 00:54:49.442
But that little bit that I place in His hand, every day again,

46
00:54:49.442 --> 00:54:54.242
where I die myself and try to do His will,

47
00:54:54.242 --> 00:55:00.442
shapes me and molds me, so that I increasingly resemble Him.

48
00:55:00.442 --> 00:55:03.442
And that is day by day by day.

49
00:55:03.442 --> 00:55:06.442
And this is actually the intention in His kingdom.

50
00:55:06.442 --> 00:55:13.242
For there can be a danger lurking, when we start building and enthusiastically engaging in His kingdom,

51
00:55:13.242 --> 00:55:16.242
that we build on the foundation of Jesus,

52
00:55:16.242 --> 00:55:18.442
where I might be building something,

53
00:55:18.442 --> 00:55:20.842
where we are building for ourselves.

54
00:55:20.842 --> 00:55:22.842
That is not the intention.

55
00:55:22.842 --> 00:55:25.242
It is His kingdom.

56
00:55:25.242 --> 00:55:27.942
And it must truly be done His way.

57
00:55:27.942 --> 00:55:30.442
It cannot be otherwise.

58
00:55:30.442 --> 00:55:34.842
Everything we build, and I am not talking about that construction site behind here,

59
00:55:34.842 --> 00:55:37.642
but everything we build for His kingdom,

60
00:55:37.642 --> 00:55:40.242
is inspired by the Father.

61
00:55:40.242 --> 00:55:43.642
It has not entered the thoughts of men.

62
00:55:43.642 --> 00:55:46.442
And it is truly to be hoped that he does not later have to discover,

63
00:55:46.442 --> 00:55:48.442
that we have built an enterprise for ourselves on the foundation of Jesus himself, that I have written down.

64
00:55:48.442 --> 00:55:52.042
I find that a very important thought.

65
00:55:52.042 --> 00:55:54.442
Shall we take ourselves into his service, for his building plans?

66
00:55:54.442 --> 00:55:58.442
Or are we busy for ourselves?

67
00:55:58.442 --> 00:56:01.842
From ourselves, that building project can never succeed.

68
00:56:01.842 --> 00:56:04.642
It has no chance of success.

69
00:56:04.642 --> 00:56:06.442
Only through the resurrection power of Christ.

70
00:56:06.442 --> 00:56:09.642
And walking in his resurrection power, every day anew through faith in Jesus.

71
00:56:09.642 --> 00:56:14.242
Only through that true cornerstone on which his church is built.

72
00:56:14.242 --> 00:56:18.042
And that can also be from generation to generation.

73
00:56:18.042 --> 00:56:21.042
Therefore, it is also important to be careful towards our next generation.

74
00:56:21.042 --> 00:56:27.442
That we carry this message of this gospel with us.

75
00:56:27.442 --> 00:56:33.042
For just as a child takes over a business from his dad or mom,

76
00:56:33.042 --> 00:56:40.442
he must know what to do with it.

77
00:56:40.442 --> 00:56:42.842
He must know those thoughts, he must know what it is built on.

78
00:56:42.842 --> 00:56:46.442
The way of building and the strategy behind the building plan.

79
00:56:46.442 --> 00:56:51.042
And in the same way, it is also important that we, as we give,

80
00:56:51.042 --> 00:56:54.442


81
00:56:54.442 --> 00:56:57.442
that we also think of our children, that we teach our children

82
00:56:57.442 --> 00:57:00.642
to return to that good good Father.

83
00:57:00.842 --> 00:57:05.642
To know that there is nothing of ours in it, but that we may keep 90%.

84
00:57:05.642 --> 00:57:10.242
To be a good steward for His kingdom with that.

85
00:57:10.242 --> 00:57:12.642
And I think it is very good to do that.

86
00:57:12.642 --> 00:57:17.642
When we talk about building and about generations, let us keep this in mind.

87
00:57:17.642 --> 00:57:20.842
For our own hearts, but also for our children.

88
00:57:20.842 --> 00:57:24.642
This for our children, that they will embrace those same thoughts.

89
00:57:24.642 --> 00:57:29.042
For it is indeed a work of the Spirit, which we cannot simply force ourselves.

90
00:57:29.042 --> 00:57:32.442
That is why it is good to pray for our children every day, also for this.

91
00:57:32.442 --> 00:57:35.442
And perhaps it is also beautiful to stand in these thoughts,

92
00:57:35.442 --> 00:57:39.242
and also the offering that we may bring for today,

93
00:57:39.242 --> 00:57:43.242
that we may return that to our good good Father.

94
00:57:43.242 --> 00:57:45.042
Father, thank You very much.

95
00:57:45.042 --> 00:57:47.842
Lord, You do not have any grandchildren, Lord.

96
00:57:47.842 --> 00:57:53.442
You walk with each of us, also with our children, a unique path, together with You.

97
00:57:53.442 --> 00:57:58.842
And how important, Lord, it is to walk and act, Lord, in Your light.

98
00:57:58.842 --> 00:58:03.442
Lord, and as we walk and act together in the light where the Father is,

99
00:58:03.442 --> 00:58:05.642
then we are ultimately connected with each other.

100
00:58:05.642 --> 00:58:09.642
In Christ Jesus our Lord, for He has paid the offering.

101
00:58:09.642 --> 00:58:13.242
And we want to give you all praise, honor, and glory, Lord, with the offering.

102
00:58:13.242 --> 00:58:15.442
Lord, what we bring back to you.

103
00:58:15.442 --> 00:58:18.442
Lord, for this is true righteousness in Christ.

104
00:58:18.442 --> 00:58:21.242
Lord, to do as you would do.

105
00:58:21.242 --> 00:58:24.042
Lord, and I thank you, Lord, that you bless us with that,

106
00:58:24.042 --> 00:58:26.442
and also bless our descendants in that.

107
00:58:26.442 --> 00:58:29.642
That we may give it for you, for each other,

108
00:58:29.642 --> 00:58:33.042
and also for our descendants in the name of King Jesus. Amen.

109
00:58:41.642 --> 00:58:43.642
Are you ready for the Word of God?

110
00:58:43.642 --> 00:58:45.642
Yes.

111
00:58:45.642 --> 00:58:48.642
Good. Did you bring your Bible?

112
00:58:48.642 --> 00:58:51.042
Please show your Bible.

113
00:58:51.042 --> 00:58:53.842
Just checking.

114
00:58:54.042 --> 00:58:55.442
Very good.

115
00:58:55.442 --> 00:58:58.842
Praise God, let us be a culture...

116
00:58:58.842 --> 00:59:03.442
...of people who read from God's Word.

117
00:59:05.442 --> 00:59:10.242
Normally I always have the Bible verses on paper in my folder,

118
00:59:10.242 --> 00:59:14.042
but I also want to set a good example by teaching from God's Word.

119
00:59:14.042 --> 00:59:16.442
It's both the same.

120
00:59:16.442 --> 00:59:19.042
But when I say, bring your Bible, you can easily say,

121
00:59:19.042 --> 00:59:20.842
Yes, I just do it from my phone.

122
00:59:20.842 --> 00:59:22.442
Yes, yes, I read from the screen.

123
00:59:22.442 --> 00:59:26.242
But there are reasons behind everything we say.

124
00:59:26.242 --> 00:59:28.042
Read your Bible, pray every day.

125
00:59:28.042 --> 00:59:29.842
Be natural.

126
00:59:29.842 --> 00:59:33.242
Make it a habit to engage with God's Word.

127
00:59:33.242 --> 00:59:36.042
And yes, that can be an app.

128
00:59:36.042 --> 00:59:42.442
Only, one of the downsides of the modern age we live in,

129
00:59:42.442 --> 00:59:46.842
is that the Bible can be reduced to a daily app

130
00:59:46.842 --> 00:59:49.842
that comes in from YouVersion.

131
00:59:49.842 --> 00:59:51.842
And then it's ping, oh yes, nice.

132
00:59:51.842 --> 00:59:54.242
And that is an encouraging Bible verse, always.

133
00:59:54.242 --> 00:59:56.242
And then you say, I have read my Bible,

134
00:59:56.242 --> 01:00:01.242
but God's Word is so much more than just a ping. Amen.

135
01:00:01.242 --> 01:00:04.042
You all need to wake up.

136
01:00:04.042 --> 01:00:10.642
We are nicely engaged in Acts, in the book of Acts.

137
01:00:10.642 --> 01:00:15.642
And today I want to read from 1 Corinthians.

138
01:00:15.642 --> 01:00:21.042
Because last week we talked from Acts, chapter 2.

139
01:00:21.042 --> 01:00:26.442
And in Acts, chapter 2, we talked together about speaking in the tongues of the Spirit.

140
01:00:26.442 --> 01:00:28.842
Who can still remember last week?

141
01:00:28.842 --> 01:00:32.642
Yes? So much happens during a week that when you say sometimes,

142
01:00:32.642 --> 01:00:36.242
what did you do yesterday, is it nice...

143
01:00:36.242 --> 01:00:37.842
Ah...

144
01:00:37.842 --> 01:00:41.842
So, we still know where we left off last week. Amen?

145
01:00:41.842 --> 01:00:43.842
Amen?

146
01:00:51.042 --> 01:00:59.842
The book of Acts is, shall I say, the genesis of the New Testament.

147
01:00:59.842 --> 01:01:04.642
The book of Acts is the origin of the congregation,

148
01:01:04.642 --> 01:01:09.042
and the things that the Holy Spirit does to build the congregation.

149
01:01:09.042 --> 01:01:13.842
The coming of the Holy Spirit was of vital importance,

150
01:01:13.842 --> 01:01:16.842
to be able to spread the gospel.

151
01:01:16.842 --> 01:01:20.442
The coming of the Holy Spirit was not solely intended for you,

152
01:01:20.442 --> 01:01:25.242
even though we are blessed as a foretaste with the Holy Spirit.

153
01:01:25.242 --> 01:01:30.442
Can I get an amen from someone who feels blessed with the Holy Spirit?

154
01:01:30.442 --> 01:01:34.642
Amen, amen. Yes.

155
01:01:34.642 --> 01:01:38.642
And what we then see happening in Acts, chapter 2,

156
01:01:38.642 --> 01:01:43.242
is that the outpouring of the Holy Spirit causes a miracle.

157
01:01:43.242 --> 01:01:47.042
The first thing the Holy Spirit does is fill the people,

158
01:01:47.042 --> 01:01:53.042
and there were tongues of fire seen in the room, in the upper room,

159
01:01:53.042 --> 01:01:56.642
about 120 people were gathered together and they were praying,

160
01:01:56.642 --> 01:02:01.442
and I believe with all my heart that they were shouting and praying.

161
01:02:01.442 --> 01:02:05.842
for the return of their Lord and for their King, King Jesus.

162
01:02:05.842 --> 01:02:08.242
For Jesus said, I will come back,

163
01:02:08.242 --> 01:02:12.842
but all those days that I am not with you, I will be with you, says Jesus.

164
01:02:12.842 --> 01:02:15.842
And that is the promise of the Holy Spirit.

165
01:02:15.842 --> 01:02:22.842
The Spirit of Jesus has come upon the believers, upon all of us.

166
01:02:22.842 --> 01:02:25.842
And we talked about this last week.

167
01:02:25.842 --> 01:02:29.842
The first thing the Holy Spirit did was a miracle.

168
01:02:29.842 --> 01:02:33.442
Namely, He filled all the believers, that is miracle 1.

169
01:02:33.442 --> 01:02:38.242
And secondly, He gave a gift to all the believers.

170
01:02:38.242 --> 01:02:43.642
And that is, that they all began to pray in the languages of the Spirit.

171
01:02:43.642 --> 01:02:46.442
We talked about this last week.

172
01:02:46.442 --> 01:02:50.842
And I have laid down that I believe with all my heart,

173
01:02:50.842 --> 01:02:54.642
that the Bible teaches that the languages of the Spirit,

174
01:02:54.642 --> 01:02:58.842
both the speaking of a real language as we know it,

175
01:02:58.842 --> 01:03:02.042
Dutch, French, German, Spanish,

176
01:03:02.042 --> 01:03:06.242
in all the languages as the people came together in Jerusalem,

177
01:03:06.242 --> 01:03:09.642
at that moment on pilgrimage,

178
01:03:09.642 --> 01:03:13.642
they heard that the disciples, the apostles,

179
01:03:13.642 --> 01:03:17.842
were speaking in their own language.

180
01:03:17.842 --> 01:03:22.242
And they were explaining the wonderful things of God.

181
01:03:22.242 --> 01:03:28.242
They were telling the gospel of Jesus Christ in all the languages of the world.

182
01:03:28.242 --> 01:03:31.442
And the people in Jerusalem were amazed,

183
01:03:31.442 --> 01:03:36.842
how can it be that those Galileans speak pure Arabic?

184
01:03:36.842 --> 01:03:41.442
How can it be that those Galileans were speaking pure Hindi?

185
01:03:41.442 --> 01:03:45.442
How can it be that those Galileans were speaking Lommels?

186
01:03:45.442 --> 01:03:49.442
How can it be that all those languages of the world

187
01:03:49.442 --> 01:03:54.242
were represented in those 120 people who were there?

188
01:03:54.242 --> 01:03:58.242
And the people found it a miracle and they gathered to listen.

189
01:03:58.242 --> 01:04:03.242
So the first miracle that the languages of the Spirit did,

190
01:04:03.242 --> 01:04:07.242
is the spreading of the good news of Jesus Christ.

191
01:04:07.242 --> 01:04:12.042
The Holy Spirit has come into you for the world.

192
01:04:12.042 --> 01:04:18.642
I repeat, the Holy Spirit has come into you for the world.

193
01:04:18.642 --> 01:04:23.442
If you think you can keep the Holy Spirit just for yourself, fine,

194
01:04:23.442 --> 01:04:26.442
but the Holy Spirit is greater than your heart.

195
01:04:26.442 --> 01:04:29.442
And He wants out. He wants to flow.

196
01:04:29.442 --> 01:04:33.842
He wants streams of living water to come out of your innermost being,

197
01:04:33.842 --> 01:04:40.042
so that other people can be blessed by the gifts of the Holy Spirit in you.

198
01:04:40.042 --> 01:04:42.842
And what I actually emphasized last week is,

199
01:04:42.842 --> 01:04:49.442
one, I want to teach about the fact that speaking in the languages of the Holy Spirit

200
01:04:49.442 --> 01:04:52.242
is a language for you that you do not understand,

201
01:04:52.242 --> 01:04:55.642
and what God can do with it is up to God.

202
01:04:55.642 --> 01:04:57.642
Did you all understand that?

203
01:04:57.642 --> 01:05:01.242
What God wants to do with it is up to God,

204
01:05:01.242 --> 01:05:05.242
and also I believe, I believe, that is a personal interpretation,

205
01:05:05.242 --> 01:05:11.042
I believe that it also reaches the heart of those who have opened their hearts,

206
01:05:11.042 --> 01:05:16.042
and that it will not reach the hearts of the people who are not open to it.

207
01:05:16.042 --> 01:05:20.242
That is why we also read in Acts chapter 2 that there were people who said,

208
01:05:20.242 --> 01:05:22.842
yes, those people have just drunk too much.

209
01:05:22.842 --> 01:05:26.642
I already explained last week, I believe with all my heart,

210
01:05:26.642 --> 01:05:33.842
that those people who heard their language, their pure language, would never say that.

211
01:05:33.842 --> 01:05:37.042
But it was precisely those people who only heard babbling,

212
01:05:37.042 --> 01:05:42.242
who said, yes, those people have just drunk too much.

213
01:05:42.242 --> 01:05:47.242
Today I want to address what Paul does a little later,

214
01:05:47.242 --> 01:05:52.442
for in Acts we read that we see what the Holy Spirit,

215
01:05:52.442 --> 01:05:56.042
I will just say, does for the first time in the believers,

216
01:05:56.042 --> 01:05:59.842
and there is an explosion of the gifts of the Holy Spirit,

217
01:05:59.842 --> 01:06:02.842
and the people begin to speak in new tongues,

218
01:06:02.842 --> 01:06:10.242
and the people receive that in pure languages or however.

219
01:06:10.242 --> 01:06:17.842
And then you see that the book of Acts is the narrative genre, as I have said before.

220
01:06:17.842 --> 01:06:23.042
In the book of Acts we read what happens,

221
01:06:23.042 --> 01:06:30.242
And in the letters that follow, we read how the apostles teach

222
01:06:30.242 --> 01:06:35.442
about how to deal with the gifts of the Holy Spirit,

223
01:06:35.442 --> 01:06:39.842
or how we can together form the church of Jesus Christ.

224
01:06:39.842 --> 01:06:45.442
So there is a big difference between the book of Acts and, for example, a letter to the Romans,

225
01:06:45.442 --> 01:06:46.642
do you understand what I mean?

226
01:06:46.642 --> 01:06:52.242
There is a big difference between the book of Acts and a letter to the Corinthians.

227
01:06:52.242 --> 01:06:55.842
And what Paul does in the letter to the Corinthians is,

228
01:06:55.842 --> 01:07:01.842
he gives direction to what arises in the book of Acts, particularly chapter 2

229
01:07:01.842 --> 01:07:07.242
about speaking in the tongues of the Spirit.

230
01:07:07.242 --> 01:07:15.642
When the Holy Spirit does something, we are blessed by it and taste what God can do.

231
01:07:15.642 --> 01:07:18.642
Do you know what is very human?

232
01:07:18.642 --> 01:07:21.242
That we want to continue that.

233
01:07:21.242 --> 01:07:23.242
That makes sense.

234
01:07:23.242 --> 01:07:30.042
If God gives a gift, then the next day we say we want that from yesterday.

235
01:07:30.042 --> 01:07:32.042
I want that again today.

236
01:07:32.042 --> 01:07:36.842
And that is a decent desire, that is not wrong.

237
01:07:36.842 --> 01:07:44.642
